#: ../../source/docs/soaring.rst:9
#: 1dc8265f2a2f491c82281a48f712250e
msgid "Soaring"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/soaring.rst:14
#: 13dc937a90794cf18b276b2ecc1c146a
msgid "The autonomous soaring functionality in ArduPilot allows the plane to respond to rising air current (thermals) in order to extend endurance and gain altitude with minimal use of the motor (soaring). Its full technical description is available in"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/soaring.rst:18
#: 296b459959754f72bb83d8ac91dc40b7
msgid "*S. Tabor, I. Guilliard, A. Kolobov.* `ArduSoar: an Open-Source Thermalling Controller for Resource-Constrained Autopilots <https://arxiv.org/abs/1802.08215/>`_. *International Conference on Intelligent Robots and Systems (IROS), 2018.*"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/soaring.rst:20
#: 2308f2b9990845bd8505dfbd52e140e0
msgid "Use of an airspeed sensor is strongly recommended in order to obtain optimum performance. Use without a sensor could yield unsatisfactory results. Consistent operation without an airspeed sensor is a pending future development."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/soaring.rst:24
#: 6cb76bbd770b4a3d895717b7c21b838a
msgid "This picture shows the different phases of flight when using the soaring functionality:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/soaring.rst:27
#: d532cb2b603b443696830348f544cfd8
msgid "If modes AUTO, FBWB or CRUISE are entered, and Soaring is enabled, the throttle is set to zero provided the aircraft is above :ref:`SOAR_ALT_MIN<SOAR_ALT_MIN>` altitude and the aircraft then begins gliding."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/soaring.rst:28
#: 4022264e8b7e437aa1178608576cbea2
msgid "In AUTO, if the aircraft descends to :ref:`SOAR_ALT_MIN<SOAR_ALT_MIN>` altitude, throttle is re-enabled and the aircraft will begin to climb to the altitude of the next waypoint. If that waypoint altitude is less than :ref:`SOAR_ALT_CUTOFF<SOAR_ALT_CUTOFF>` altitude, then Soaring can not begin before reaching the waypoint. If it is above :ref:`SOAR_ALT_CUTOFF<SOAR_ALT_CUTOFF>` altitude, then Soaring can occur once that altitude has been reached. In FBWB or CRUISE modes, if  :ref:`SOAR_ALT_MIN<SOAR_ALT_MIN>` altitude is reached, an RTL will be initiated, so the pilot must disable Soaring, or change to a mode other than FBWB or CRUISE to climb back above :ref:`SOAR_ALT_CUTOFF<SOAR_ALT_CUTOFF>` to begin gliding again and prevent an RTL beginning."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/soaring.rst:29
#: 2ac07cc6f02f400480ac4b398cb873dd
msgid "When the aircraft reaches :ref:`SOAR_ALT_CUTOFF<SOAR_ALT_CUTOFF>` altitude, throttle is set to zero again."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/soaring.rst:30
#: fb246fb212d4472d9df8ca7883430026
msgid "If, during gliding flight, the air is estimated to be rising at more than :ref:`SOAR_VSPEED<SOAR_VSPEED>` and the :ref:`RC switch position<soaring_rc-switch>` allows it, the aircraft will automatically enter LOITER mode. While in LOITER mode the aircraft will adjust the loiter position to better centre the thermal."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/soaring.rst:32
#: 24a1d0b6bfde4b91b4370b8017665d14
msgid "LOITER mode is exited under the following conditions:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/soaring.rst:34
#: 46d15572b7674dc38c699a8b0433f7e6
msgid ":ref:`SOAR_ALT_MAX<SOAR_ALT_MAX>` is reached."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/soaring.rst:35
#: 2582e6e6580e40a1a9e3e428c30f8937
msgid ":ref:`SOAR_ALT_MIN<SOAR_ALT_MIN>` is reached."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/soaring.rst:36
#: 82a6ad2a680a4707af0dd1c6aa8fd4ef
msgid "Flight mode is changed by the pilot."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/soaring.rst:37
#: c12f83b81d6b421e81f7d4c7c42693d7
msgid "The estimate of achievable climb rate falls below :ref:`SOAR_VSPEED<SOAR_VSPEED>`, and thermalling has lasted at least :ref:`SOAR_MIN_THML_S<SOAR_MIN_THML_S>` seconds."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/soaring.rst:39
#: 29e65eabd2d34d0093acb0c870f371ed
msgid "The aircraft drifts more than :ref:`SOAR_MAX_DRIFT<SOAR_MAX_DRIFT>` - see :ref:`Limit maximum distance from home<soaring_maximum-distance-from-home>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/soaring.rst:41
#: 104c10e2790148b19a5b2158b12ca484
msgid "The flight mode will be returned to whatever it was before LOITER was triggered. As an exception to this, if the previous mode was FBWB or CRUISE, and thermalling ended due to reaching :ref:`SOAR_ALT_MIN<SOAR_ALT_MIN>`, RTL will be triggered instead."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/soaring.rst:47
