#: 1ff67f9312fd423ea66f65135b3381ba
msgid "Mission"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/soaring.rst:66
#: 3959a574f59a489ca9ad51c21ba9dac8
msgid "The main requirement for a mission is that it take the aircraft above :ref:`SOAR_ALT_CUTOFF<SOAR_ALT_CUTOFF>` so that gliding flight is initiated. To achieve this, set the waypoints' altitude(s) above :ref:`SOAR_ALT_CUTOFF<SOAR_ALT_CUTOFF>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/soaring.rst:71
#: e1c9c888bcac425295392204fb9a5a14
msgid "TECS"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/soaring.rst:73
#: 4ca28440329c4686a3985ee4441a48f6
msgid "Set :ref:`TECS_SPDWEIGHT<TECS_SPDWEIGHT>` to 2.0. This makes sure the aircraft will glide correctly with motor off."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/soaring.rst:76
#: f5a9582df62d474882a1806dbf0bf463
msgid "Soaring Parameters"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/soaring.rst:79
#: 6b4184e9f0be436eab83535e117b233b
msgid "Enable"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/soaring.rst:81
#: d344986945ee4397b447dd9aa91b39dc
msgid "Set the parameter :ref:`SOAR_ENABLE<SOAR_ENABLE>` to 1 and refresh the parameters. This will allow the other SOAR parameters to appear in the GCS."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/soaring.rst:85
#: ../../source/docs/soaring.rst:158
#: 97c147d152ae402e9a0fab6faab4fb17
#: 12e3ce4915f540e78cec6c2714379ec5
msgid "Drag Polar"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/soaring.rst:87
#: b5c0e8dba64b47bf895ecccd57de85ef
msgid "To work out how fast the air is rising or sinking the autopilot needs to know the aircraft's sink rate for a given airspeed in still air. This is related to the drag polar of the plane and is specified using the SOAR_POLAR parameters. :ref:`SOAR_POLAR_K<SOAR_POLAR_K>` is the most important one to set initially and is calculated using the following formula:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/soaring.rst:93
#: b2d5956a52104a768afb3b102f7260f3
msgid ":ref:`SOAR_POLAR_K<SOAR_POLAR_K>` = 16*Weight/Area (weight in kg, area in metres squared)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/soaring.rst:96
#: ffa077021cf34ba1b87d8b154eccdda6
msgid ":ref:`SOAR_POLAR_K<SOAR_POLAR_K>` = 703*Weight/Area (weight in oz, area in inches squared)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/soaring.rst:99
#: 624676fbf0bb45bd801a5f7e6cdf63d4
msgid "Calculating the other parameters is explained under tuning."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/soaring.rst:104
#: 26cb85fac6814e8cb6eef5457ebf923c
msgid "RC switch (Optional)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/soaring.rst:106
#: 835d0d93199e4d76af0dea46f7ef67da
msgid "You can use a 2-position RC switch to control when the autopilot can use soaring. Use any available RC Option with ``RCx_OPTION`` value 88. The 2 positions have the following effect."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/soaring.rst:108
#: 5b1c4798de4c486d9baafd6f9adda4ca
msgid "Below 1700us. Soaring is disabled (equivalent to setting SOAR_ENABLE = 0). Throttle will be used as normal. Switching to this from either of the positions below, will disable Soaring and maintain the current flight mode."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/soaring.rst:110
#: ba506c0c9d4f40358ca222ff7958f217
msgid "Above 1700us. Fully automatic mode changes to LOITER from AUTO, FBWB or CRUISE modes in response to detected rising air, and following of rising air currents."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/soaring.rst:114
#: ac35513b758b4ea5bf485445927a48c3
msgid "Loiter radius"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/soaring.rst:116
#: 69684506bcc74016b3d2b440fa6fc0e3
msgid "The parameter :ref:`WP_LOITER_RAD<WP_LOITER_RAD>` sets how tight the loiter circle is. For thermalling it is usually best to have the aircraft fly at a 30 - 45 degree bank angle. The corresponding loiter radius can be calculated as about airspeed squared over ~10 (for 45 degrees) or ~6 (for 30 degrees), from the equation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/soaring.rst:124
#: da404c529e68415aa478770fc52a9c90
msgid "The tangent is for the desired bank angle. The resulting radius will be in meters. Use g  = 9.81 m/s/s, and velocity (v) is in m/s. For example, if the airspeed in loiter is 20m/s, then the :ref:`WP_LOITER_RAD<WP_LOITER_RAD>` should be 40m for a 45 degree bank."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/soaring.rst:126
#: 94520873726c4596965e2d274bcb1dc5
msgid "You should make sure that the limiting bank angle :ref:`ROLL_LIMIT_DEG<ROLL_LIMIT_DEG>` is set a bit larger than the desired bank angle to give some room for manoeuvring."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/soaring.rst:130
#: 95cd193edbf84804af4fe2f6fe53a80e
msgid "Set limits"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/soaring.rst:132
#: d1650bd215c2476789e6d1ce8a2d8508
msgid "Because the soaring feature can follow rising air as required to gain altitude, it is important to set limits to avoid it leaving the original flight area completely. This is especially important in windy conditions as the autopilot will try to follow thermals downwind."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/soaring.rst:135
#: 3b2aaac0c35e48d9acea7a607a128173
msgid "Altitude limits"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/soaring.rst:137
#: 7be2ca5ae6d842448cd1f5c05f9c3a85
msgid ":ref:`SOAR_ALT_MAX<SOAR_ALT_MAX>` sets the altitude you want the autopilot to stop thermalling. :ref:`SOAR_ALT_MIN<SOAR_ALT_MIN>` sets the minimum altitude you want the autopilot to descend to while gliding."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/soaring.rst:142
#: 71f3efe18f314d218820a76d99ecdb7c
msgid "Spatial limits"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/soaring.rst:144
#: ef0385a2e6f540a8a26568aaff5e29e0
msgid ":ref:`Geofence <geofencing>` can be used to constrain the physical flight area used. Set it up in the usual way."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/soaring.rst:148
#: 2e42bea1a3394f14b08b2a320048ab03
msgid "Tuning"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/soaring.rst:151
#: 89944eacbe42482aaf14ba26e3f9a23e
msgid "Triggering lift"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/soaring.rst:153
#: 57cdffb07b6c40b3aed2ba304e67fafb
msgid ":ref:`SOAR_VSPEED<SOAR_VSPEED>` controls when the mode will be changed to LOITER to begin thermalling. The default of 0.7m/s may be too low if you fly in strong conditions. Increasing this value makes the aircraft more \"picky\" about the lift it will try to circle in."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/soaring.rst:160
#: 03363406f80b493dac56ae6065ffcd3e
msgid "While the default settings for :ref:`SOAR_POLAR_B<SOAR_POLAR_B>` and :ref:`SOAR_POLAR_CD0<SOAR_POLAR_CD0>` should be OK for most foamie-style glider aircraft, improving the accuracy of these parameters will improve how your aircraft detects and centres lift. You can use `this spreadsheet <https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1WA9CXRSPBc6mFydhQ3O_2SeDrQoFH1UrdiXd0PJ-zE4/edit?usp=sharing>`__ to calculate better values from glide tests."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/soaring.rst:166
#: c64132839f18462bb34be1ac0012ee03
msgid "Time hysteresis"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/soaring.rst:168
#: 4fc539cb5bac43489bf922be001f96f1
msgid "Adding hysteresis can reduce the frequency of mode changes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/soaring.rst:170
#: f8ceb0ee78c74044a300e16d9bbe5507
msgid ":ref:`SOAR_MIN_THML_S<SOAR_MIN_THML_S>`: Minimum time to remain in LOITER once entered for a thermal before exiting due to low lift or altitude limits."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/soaring.rst:172
#: 3a93ca4e11da433da46e7b64d483f23c
msgid ":ref:`SOAR_MIN_CRSE_S<SOAR_MIN_CRSE_S>`: Minimum time to remain in glide after exiting LOITER due to low lift or altitude limits before entering LOITER mode again, or when entering Soaring initially."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/soaring.rst:175
#: 2bfe262de7bc46cd9f4c8c2a7d6b5174
msgid "TECS Tuning"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/soaring.rst:176
#: 5c21775cadf340ffb8ce843da23faf25
msgid "For best results the TECS needs to be set up to fly the aircraft at a consistent airspeed when gliding."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/soaring.rst:179
#: e98439cf506e470db2a757083fa4eb10
msgid "If your aircraft has trouble maintaining airspeed accurately you can tune it by confirming that :ref:`TECS_SPDWEIGHT<TECS_SPDWEIGHT>` is set to 2.0, :ref:`SOAR_ENABLE<SOAR_ENABLE>` to 1 and set :ref:`SOAR_VSPEED<SOAR_VSPEED>` to a large number, say 50.0, or use the :ref:`RC switch<soaring_rc-switch>` to inhibit mode changes. This means that the aircraft will glide but will never begin thermalling. Set :ref:`SOAR_ALT_CUTOFF<SOAR_ALT_CUTOFF>` to an altitude high enough to allow a good length of time to be spent gliding."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/soaring.rst:186
#: 57c6557dfc3a400d983f80fa2fc7ca75
msgid "Launch the aircraft and put it in AUTO mode. It should climb to :ref:`SOAR_ALT_CUTOFF<SOAR_ALT_CUTOFF>` and then begin a gliding descent. Watch the telemetry graphs or look at the Dataflash logs after the flight. Is the aircraft maintaining the demanded airspeed? The actual and demanded airspeed can be seen in the onboard log as ``TECS.sp`` and ``TECS.spdem``, and via telemetry you can use ``NAV_CONTROLLER_OUTPUT.aspd_error``. Problems can usually be fixed by increasing ``PTCH2SRV_IMAX`` and :ref:`TECS_INTEG_GAIN<TECS_INTEG_GAIN>` to achieve good airspeed tracking in gliding flight."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/soaring.rst:193
#: 0ec98f688eef4e3dbd2a249fda797968
msgid "Notes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/soaring.rst:196
#: b537e6345304493fbf61fc52947a6599
msgid "MAVLINK Telemetry"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/soaring.rst:198
#: 599fd927d82d4c7ca095759c2a261675
msgid "Currently, the only effect on telemetry is that when soaring is active the climb rate item (VFR_HUD.climb) is altered. Rather that the estimated vertical speed of the aircraft, the estimated vertical speed of the air mass is sent. This field is used by Mission Planner and OpenTX radios to produce vario audio output."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/soaring.rst:201
#: 58a0a9b4bdcf47f5be9f92f2fa59cb15
msgid "Use of TECS synthetic airspeed"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/soaring.rst:203
#: ff1c1a010d734aa0ab630f67e4cec66b
msgid "If your plane can't accommodate an airspeed sensor, it is possible to use the TECS synthetic airspeed estimate :ref:`TECS_SYNAIRSPEED<TECS_SYNAIRSPEED>`. Make sure you read the warning regarding this feature before deciding to use it. To use this feature, set the parameter :ref:`TECS_SYNAIRSPEED<TECS_SYNAIRSPEED>` to 1."
msgstr ""
